  "enhanced_information": "Mutation of tumor suppressor genes can lead to loss of their normal function, contributing to carcinogenesis. Oncogenes behave dominantly by promoting cell proliferation. The RB gene is a tumor suppressor gene that can contribute to carcinogenesis when mutated. The RAS gene is an oncogene that can also contribute to carcinogenesis when mutated. The evidence path linking Tumor Suppressor Genes with Retinoblastoma Genes supports the role of tumor suppressor genes in regulating cell growth."
